{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Who will give.</b> Scripture does not say \"Who will give to me\" but rather \"Who will give to them\"; therefore להם is written after \"and their heart shall be this.\" Know that the root of all deeds and motions is the decrees of HaShem, and all beings under the heavens—their force and their outcomes are according to the supernal configuration, together with the roots below, and likewise with the composite beings, and likewise according to their motions day by day and time by time, for there will always be change, as the author of Sefer Yetzirah explained. The particulars receive from the universals according to their outcomes, and by virtue of the power of the universals they are able to alter slightly in outcome. This is the meaning of \"and YHWH strengthened Pharaoh's heart,\" and elsewhere \"his heart and his servants' heart was hardened\"—all of it is truth. Therefore he says: \"I know, HaShem, that man's way is not his own,\" and he says: \"Why do You lead us astray, HaShem, from Your way?\" And Moses said: \"and you shall choose life.\" And since HaShem does not withhold good—behold, He loves to bestow good—and Scripture spoke in the language of mortals: מי יתן."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "The first Scriptural quotation is from Jeremiah 10:23, the second from Isaiah 63:17; the identity of the Hebrew ואומר citations is resolved by the verse content."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:32.936245167Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}